{"company":{"id":"slack","name":"Slack","accent":"#611f69","asset":"messages","verb":"send a message"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"Chat app","kind":"client","blurb":"Sends and displays messages.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Slack app on your phone or laptop. Tapping send a message starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"gw","title":"Connection gateway","kind":"api","blurb":"Keeps an always-on link so messages feel instant.","depth":1,"story":"Chat on Slack keeps a live wire open so bubbles appear without a full page load each time."},{"id":"lb","title":"Load balancer","kind":"api","blurb":"Spreads millions of sockets.","depth":1,"story":"Millions of open chats are spread across many connection machines so one box is not a single point of failure."},{"id":"auth","title":"Identity","kind":"auth","blurb":"Who owns this device and chat list.","depth":2,"story":"Before Slack shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"presence","title":"Presence","kind":"service","blurb":"Online, typing, last seen.","depth":2,"story":"Green dot / typing… is a high-churn signal. It is not stored like a 10-year message archive."},{"id":"msg","title":"Message service","kind":"service","blurb":"Stores and routes a chat item.","depth":2,"story":"The router for a chat item: persist it, send it, retry if the other phone is asleep."},{"id":"media","title":"Media service","kind":"service","blurb":"Images, voice notes, files.","depth":3,"story":"Photos and voice notes are a separate path from short text. They are large messages."},{"id":"cache","title":"Session / unread cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Recent chats and badges.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Slack keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"msgdb","title":"Message store","kind":"db","blurb":"History, often partitioned by chat id.","depth":4,"story":"Years of chats, split by conversation. Not the same store as group member lists."},{"id":"userdb","title":"User / group DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Rosters and permissions.","depth":4,"story":"Your continue-watching / saved list lives here. It is tiny compared with messages, and it is queried often."},{"id":"blob","title":"Media store","kind":"blob","blurb":"Attachments, not the text rows.","depth":4,"story":"The warehouse for large messages. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” Slack points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"queue","title":"Delivery queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"Retry when the other phone is offline.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at send a message. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"push","title":"Push notifications","kind":"workers","blurb":"Wakes the other phone when a chat arrives.","depth":5,"story":"Background helpers at Slack. They retry if something fails. They are not sitting on the button you just pressed."},{"id":"e2e","title":"Keys / E2E (if any)","kind":"auth","blurb":"Device keys; server may not read bodies.","depth":6,"story":"Before Slack shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Public stickers and large downloads.","depth":6,"story":"On Slack, bulky messages are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"workspace-search","title":"Workspace search","kind":"service","blurb":"Indexes permitted messages and files while respecting workspace access.","depth":6,"story":"Indexes permitted messages and files while respecting workspace access."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"lb","label":"open socket"},{"from":"lb",